encyclopedia :unmaking do
  name "Unmaking"
  summary "Unmaking destroys the coherence that lets an object, body, or constructed system continue as one thing."
  kind :ability
  subkind :resonant_effect
  status :complete
  log "2026-08-31 — Kept one focused-tier spell ending one person-sized physical subject. Unclosing became the broad interruption of an active broad-band working because it leaves the working's material coherence intact; city, army, and phenomenon-scale work remains the Unmaker mantle's reach."
  log "2026-09-23 — Replaced the closing comparison with Unclosing by the demolition crews, cordon workers and killers who use Unmaking, how few teachers will take a student, how a thin field lets a working fail partway and what losing a sense for hours costs them."
  topics :resonance, :danger, :catastrophe, :"structural-freq", :subject_resonance
  prevalence :rare
  available_globally

  tier :focused
  effect "End the coherence of one person-sized object, creature, machine, barrier, or joined structure that the practitioner can perceive as one physical subject"
  limits "The spell leaves all matter and prior consequences in place, cannot target abstractions, and follows the actual boundary of the coherent subject rather than the boundary the practitioner hoped to name"
  consequence "The sense or trained faculty by which the practitioner perceived the subject goes dark for several hours; using an uncertain boundary can include connected supports, occupants, or active systems in the unmaking"

  descriptive_identity(
    signs: "The subject separates without impact or heat. Joined matter becomes loose material, active fields go silent, and coordinated parts cease recognizing one another."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    Unmaking attacks the fact that one person-sized physical subject's parts are acting together. A lock becomes separate pins, springs, and housing. A weapon loses the agreement among charge, barrel, sight, and hand. A joined barrier becomes loose material. A living body becomes tissue that no longer coordinates life. The relationships that made the subject whole simply end, with no blast.

    The remains stay. An ended field leaves charged glass and heat where its coherence had contained them. A machine becomes disconnected components that continue moving according to their momentum. Unmaking can remove a threat and release every hazard that threat was holding.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "Naming the Whole"
    The practitioner must perceive a coherent subject. A visible panel may be part of a larger pressure door; naming the panel incorrectly can take its guides and seal with it. Occupants and attached tools remain separate unless the target's operation has made them part of one active system. Beliefs, offices, debts, and nations have no single physical coherence for the spell to seize.

    The spell takes the faculty used to perceive its subject for several hours: sight after a visible machine, load sense after a structure, signal hearing after a signal-bound mechanism. #{ref :unmaker, "The Unmaker"} can destroy coherence at the scale of cities, armies, great creatures, and sustained phenomena, and its losses do not return.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :people, heading: "Who Is Taught, and Who Learns Anyway"
    Few teachers will take an Unmaking student. The ones who do are mostly demolition masters and cordon veterans, and they start the student on old locks and cracked crockery, asking for a full account of every part before each cast. A student who names a lock and takes the door hinge with it goes back to the beginning. Most practitioners have spent a long time on #{encyclopedia_ref :unclosing, "Unclosing"}, which stops a broad working and leaves its material whole, before a teacher trusts them with the spell that takes the material apart.

    An unmaker casts through a tuned ringglass blade or rod laid against the subject, and the focused working draws hard for an instant. In a thin field, or during #{encyclopedia_ref :drawdown, "drawdown"}, the working can fail partway, leaving a subject half-coherent: a door that hangs in its frame with its seal gone, a machine still turning with its governor unmade. Demolition crews call for the local foundry to stand down before an unmaking, and many teachers refuse to let a student cast at all on flat ground.

    The honest work is demolition, salvage, and cordon clearance: taking down a leaning wall without shaking the ones beside it, freeing a trapped crew by unmaking the pressure door that pinned them, ending a dangerous relic mechanism in place. Gate crews in some settlements keep an unmaker for the day a hostile machine comes through the gate. Unmaking is also a way to kill a person with no mark on them, and everyone who teaches it knows the students who came for that reason.

    The practitioner goes blind, deaf to load, or band-deaf for hours afterward, depending on how they saw the subject. That makes an unmaker at a rescue a liability for the rest of the shift, led by the arm to the rest line. It also leaves them exposed after a killing. A practitioner who unmade a rival's guard by sight in a crowded market is found, often enough, sitting on the curb nearby with their hands over their eyes.
  PROSE
end
